{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>And he called, etc.</b> They expound that אריה is חבקוק by gematria, but the correct view in my eyes is that it lacks a כף, like אש אוכלה (Deuteronomy 4:24) [i.e., כאריה], and the sense is: and the watchman called like a lion with a loud voice:" "<b>Upon the watchtower, Adonai, I stand continually.</b> And the sense is: to seek a vision."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 21, :notes {0 "Resolved the singular 'they expound' (דרש, impersonal) as referring to rabbinic exegetes; no named interlocutor given."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:54:30.461549828Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}